d in Franklin, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David H. Dupuy | CEO, President & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 35 people. Revenue per employee of $3.5M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 30%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.0M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $294K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Community Healthcare Trust Inco is a small-cap real estate business with a $423M market cap on $121M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +30% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $36M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 11.06\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 12.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 55% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 26% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Survey: National Health Investors (NYSE:NHI) & Community Healthcare Trust (NYSE:CHCT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/head-to-head-survey-national-health-investors-nysenhi-community-healthcare-trust-nysechct.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546908.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.941,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Community Healthcare Trust (CHCT) a Great Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028056/is-community-healthcare-trust-chct-a-great-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_2-3028056","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794427682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"ti